 became MASTER again (priority 200) on both groups, node2 returned to BACKUP, and node3->node4 connectivity remained intact.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-4320468f215b475a\",\"cmd-e32573dca6cc4e0e\",\"cmd-79f465f73998493e\"]}],\"confidence\":0.9,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.95,\"summary\":\"Executor's state-changing commands map cleanly to task requirements: VRRP/interface configuration on node1/node2 (committed and saved), static IP/route configuration on node3/node4 via nmcli, a bounded link-down/link-up test on node1's eth1/eth2 (fully restored within the same session, used to demonstrate failover and preemption), and the mandatory sequential reboot of all four nodes with pre/post verification. No unnecessary or unreverted mutations were found; failed commands (29 of 89) were read-only diagnostic/discovery attempts (e.g. failed 'show configuration commands' syntax probes, transient connection-timeout polling during reboots) that did not mutate state.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-a66777eedb2947a9\",\"cmd-4320468f215b475a\",\"cmd-d5e70d442713421c\",\"cmd-697773dda76649cc\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"The executor configured VRRP (NET-A/NET-B) on node1 (priority 200) and node2 (priority 100) providing a single floating VIP gateway (10.10.10.254) that node3 uses to reach node4, and demonstrated node1-down failover to node2 with continuous connectivity, followed by preemption back to node1. All four nodes were restarted per the mandatory protocol with verified boot-identity change and recovered VRRP/IP/route state. The only gap is that the node2-down (backup router) failure scenario was not explicitly exercised with a live ping during outage, though node2 was rebooted and recovered correctly.\",\"limitations\":[\"No ping-during-outage evidence was captured for the node2 restart window, so the 'backup router down' failover path is only indirectly evidenced via VRRP-group state, not a live traffic test.\",\"VyOS 'show configuration commands' introspection failed repeatedly